      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To resolve the issue, I would suggest checking the temperature settings. Polyester typically requires a heat setting of around 300-320°F (150-160°C) for optimal sublimation transfer. Ensure that the heat press is at the correct temperature, as a lower temperature may not penetrate the fabric adequately. Additionally, monitor the pressure settings to make sure they're not too low, as this can cause the ink to spread and blur.",
