    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we checked the temps and theyre definitely hitting 315f consistently. pressure seems okay too, the machine is applying even force across the plate. i'm confused because the ink is vivid on the paper but once it hits the textile it just looks dim. could it be something with the sublimation time or the way the ink is reacting to the heat during the transfer? maybe the heat isn't 'holding' long enough for the gas to fully bond?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
