      "content": "You're on the right track. The sublimation time might be a factor. The ink and substrate need time to chemically bond, and a sufficiently long transfer time is essential. Check your sublimation time and ensure it's at least 60-90 seconds, as some polyester fabrics can benefit from longer bonding times. This allows the gas to fully diffuse and bond with the fabric.",
